35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, the clay risk is real, but the eastern avenue planting is the real warning. Half dead in two years.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the firms confirm the clay risk, but the phasing notes say we can hoard the south while keeping the park open.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, the ledger is brutal. Planted ground costs triple to maintain, and the gap is widening. That’s a huge long-term hit.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, that triple cost is a nightmare. But my roll check shows only seven staff left; we simply cannot afford that upkeep.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Mio, the heat readings confirm your cost fears. The capped culvert doubled drainage callouts, and the site runs hotter than nearby streets.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, the drainage data is damning. If the ground is already failing, adding more water features is asking for trouble.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the clay is a problem, but the phasing notes are good news. We can hoard the south in stages without closing the park.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, that’s the nightmare I feared! With only seven staff, we can’t afford triple upkeep. We need a plan that’s cheap to maintain, not just cheap to build.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, exactly. With seven staff, we can’t absorb triple costs. I need a plan that fits the current rota, not one that demands a new department.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the drainage data is critical. The capped culvert doubled callouts, and heat readings are high. We must design for the ground’s actual behavior, not just aesthetics.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, the phasing is useful, but the clay means any deep work is a gamble. I’m leaning toward whatever survived the last decade.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, deep work is risky, but shallow planting is viable. The firms quote ordinary rates for that, so we can proceed without the slippage gamble.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I hear you, but the habitat fund only pays for planting and water, not hard surfaces. If we ignore that, we’re paying full price for everything.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, that fund restriction is a trap. If it only covers planting, we’re left footing the bill for everything else. We need a plan that fits our tiny staff, not just the fund’s rules.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the drainage data is critical. The capped culvert doubled callouts, and heat readings are high. We must design for the ground’s actual behavior, not just aesthetics.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, the fund terms are a constraint, not a solution. I still judge by what survived. The basin held; the apron failed. I want durability, not just planting.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, durability is key, but the clay limits deep foundations. Shallow planting is the only safe, affordable path forward.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, but the ledger says planting is triple the cost! If the fund doesn’t cover it, we’re bankrupt. I need a plan that’s cheap to keep, not just to build.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the fund covers the planting, but the staff can’t. We need a plan that doesn’t require a new department.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Mio, the heat data proves the ground is already failing. We can’t ignore the drainage reality just to save money.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
